  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="n0abc1605ede544e1ab8c45503b83a543b232">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#Imp"/>
    <rdfs:label>MQI_MM_EarthMortarJoints</rdfs:label>
    <ns3:isRuleEnabled rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</ns3:isRuleEnabled>
    <rdfs:comment>If a wall has a representative volume element which has a pattern which has dominant pattern entities ‘earth mortar joints’, then the value of MQI Mortar Quality is equal to ‘0’ for vertical loads, ‘0’ for out of plane loads and ‘0’ for in plane loads.</rdfs:comment>
    <ns1:body rdf:nodeID="n0abc1605ede544e1ab8c45503b83a543b237"/>
    <ns1:head rdf:nodeID="n0abc1605ede544e1ab8c45503b83a543b241"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="n0abc1605ede544e1ab8c45503b83a543b709">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#Imp"/>
    <rdfs:label>MQI_MM_RubbleStones_DryJoints</rdfs:label>
    <ns3:isRuleEnabled rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</ns3:isRuleEnabled>
    <rdfs:comment>If a wall has a representative volume element which has a pattern which has dominant pattern entities ‘rubble stones’, and dominant pattern entities ‘dry joints’, then the value of MQI Unit Shape is equal to ‘0’ for vertical loads, ‘0’ for out of plane loads and ‘0’ for in plane loads.</rdfs:comment>
    <ns1:body rdf:nodeID="n0abc1605ede544e1ab8c45503b83a543b715"/>
    <ns1:head rdf:nodeID="n0abc1605ede544e1ab8c45503b83a543b720"/>
  </rdf:Description>
